Step 1: Create Role-Specific Pre-Approved Tables
In the Supabase SQL Editor, create separate whitelist tables (pre_approved_admins, pre_approved_academic_heads, and pre_approved_system_admins) to store pre-authorized staff credentials securely.
Step 2: Create Role-Specific Active Personnel Tables
Create the corresponding active user tables (admins, academic_heads, and system_admins) with unique personnel numbers to store registered accounts.
Step 3: Enable Strict RLS and Keep Tables Private
Keep Row Level Security (RLS) enabled on all tables without granting any public/anonymous read policies, ensuring raw whitelist data cannot be queried directly from the frontend.
Step 4: Create Secure Postgres RPC Verification Functions
Write secure database RPC functions (SECURITY DEFINER) that take the activation input parameters, check the correct pre-approved role table internally on the backend, and return a secure match status.
Step 5: Initialize Supabase Client Configuration
Create supabase-config.js using your Supabase Project URL and public anon key, and update script references in admin-home.html.
Step 6: Maintain Form Validation and Formatting Logic
Keep client-side auto-capitalization on blur and live password criteria checks (8–12 characters, uppercase letter, number, and underscore) in admin-home.js.
Step 7: Implement Secure Activation via RPC
Update the activation form submission listener in admin-home.js to call the secure Supabase RPC function instead of querying pre-approved tables directly from the client.
Step 8: Implement Auth Sign-Up and Active Record Insertion
Upon successful RPC verification, call supabase.auth.signUp(), generate the 8-digit MyAtlas personnel number, and insert the user record into the correct active role table (admins, academic_heads, or system_admins).
Step 9: Configure Welcome Email Trigger
Set up your email trigger (via Supabase Edge Functions or database triggers) to send the generated personnel number to the user's email upon activation.
Step 10: Implement Sign-In Verification Logic
Update the sign-in form submission listener in admin-home.js to authenticate via supabase.auth.signInWithPassword() and cross-verify credentials against the corresponding active role table before redirecting to admin.html.
